## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)
- ta-a #1. “Courts currently generally impose about 3 months / 4 months / 6 months” is the advertising-rule sentence R3 tells this lane to soften. The published Tamil already says some judgments imposed about those terms and that the term is not a usual or guaranteed result. Restoring பொதுவாக would put a typical sentence length back in front of the reader.
- ta-a #7. Restoring அதிகபட்ச puts “maximum compensation” back. R3 already replaced that with the compensation the facts and evidence support, and the Tamil sentence is that form.
- ta-a verdict, “கொள்கையளவில்” as a stock opener. In these columns it is the legal “in principle / as a general rule, subject to the exception that follows” (English “in principle”, “as a general rule”). About 48 instances. Replacing them with a bare “generally” would drop that qualifier. Not swept.
- ta-b verdict, every instruction ending on உறுதிப்படுத்துங்கள். That verb is the ordinary Tamil for the English “confirm”, which the source repeats. Only the one stiff closer quoted in the verdict (“பொருளுக்குப் பொருள் மீண்டும் உறுதிப்படுத்த”) was rewritten.
- ta-b #14. The heading gap is in the English source. It is not a Tamil numbering error to close on this lane.
- ta-a #17–#18 and ta-b #24. Lakh grouping and spelling out TWD 1.57M are standing skips. The bio figure is pinned. The checker does not parse 30,00,000 or 15,79,589.
